 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-119ny', 'engagement', 'About 4 p. m. July 2 opened what is said to be the grandest cannonade of the war, lasting about five hours; about 9 p. m. the 119th and 58th New York led by Krzyzanowski charged to save the battery', 'R260', q='About 4 p. m. opened what is said to be the grandest cannonade', w='About 4 p. m.; about 9 p. m.', t='1863-07-02T16:00', d='1863-07-02', ap=True, pp='the cemetery position; the battery on East Cemetery Hill', gz='GZ-005', lbl='WL2', cf=['NT1'], note='Willis puts the night charge at about 9 p. m.'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-119ny', 'night_position', 'During the night of July 2 the regiment took position opposite the cemetery in a field and remained during July 3', 'R260', q='to take position opposite the cemetery, in a field', w='during the night (July 2)', d='1863-07-02', pp='a field opposite the cemetery', gz='GZ-004', note='Covers July 3. Note: Willis dates the cannonade of July 3 with blanks ("from — a. m. until — p. m.").'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-119ny', 'movement', 'About 8 a. m. July 4 the 119th NY and 26th Wisconsin made a reconnaissance in an easterly direction toward York for about 2 miles, taking many prisoners, then returned', 'R260', q='in an easterly direction toward York for the distance of about 2 miles', w='about 8 a. m.', t='1863-07-04T08:00', d='1863-07-04', ap=True, pp='easterly toward York, about 2 miles', rd='toward York'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-82oh', 'position', '82nd Ohio on July 1 was assigned a position on the left of the Second Brigade in the north of the town; fell back through the town and placed west of and near the cemetery building, where it remained until the evening of July 5', 'R261', q='I placed the regiment west of and near that building', w='(evening of July 1 to July 5)', pp='west of and near the cemetery building', gz='GZ-004', note='"That building" = the cemetery building (gatehouse) per the preceding sentence.'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-75pa', 'departure', '75th Pennsylvania left camp at 5 a. m. July 1 and proceeded to Gettysburg', 'R262', q='At 5 a. m. we left camp, and proceeded to Gettysburg', w='At 5 a. m.', t='1863-07-01T05:00', pp='camp at Emmitsburg', note='Agrees with Willis (about 5 a. m.); Schurz says the division left at 7.'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-75pa', 'arrival_road', '75th Pennsylvania arrived at Gettysburg at "1.30 a. m." (printed; evidently 1.30 p. m.) and was ordered to the north side of the town, 82nd Ohio on its left and 119th NY on its right', 'R262', q='to the north side of the town, where the regiment was placed as follows', w='at 1.30 a. m. (printed)', pp='the north side of the town', gz='GZ-072', cf=['XH1'], ocr=True, note='Printed "We arrived there at 1.30 a. m." The a. m. is impossible after a 5 a. m. start; t_iso left null. Not corrected.'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-75pa', 'engagement', 'About 2 o\'clock the whole brigade advanced nearly half a mile through fences under musketry, charged in a wheat-field, then fell back to an orchard and the town', 'R262', q='About 2 o\'clock, the whole brigade advanced nearly one-half mile', w='About 2 o\'clock', t='1863-07-01T14:00', ap=True, pp='north of the town, a wheat-field half a mile out', gz='GZ-072'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-75pa', 'night_position', 'A new line was formed behind the town; the regiment placed in a corn-field behind a stone wall below the Evergreen Cemetery, 82nd Ohio on its right and the First Brigade on its left', 'R262', q='behind a stone wall, below the Evergreen Cemetery', w='(evening of July 1)', pp='a corn-field behind a stone wall below the Evergreen Cemetery', gz='GZ-004', note='Cemetery unspecified wall; Evergreen Cemetery gatehouse used as the nearest gazetteer anchor.'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-26wi', 'arrival_road', '26th Wisconsin arrived with the brigade at Gettysburg about 3 p. m. July 1 and was ordered at once to the front on the extreme right of the brigade', 'R263', q='the regiment arrived with the rest of your command', w='About 3 p. m.', t='1863-07-01T15:00', ap=True, pp='the village of Gettysburg; the extreme right of the brigade', gz='GZ-072', lbl='JC1', cf=['XH1', 'DK1', 'WL1'], note='Colonel Jacobs was absent on sick leave and reports "as stated to me by officers". Hour well after the other regiments of the brigade (Ledig, Willis).'),
 c('us-11c-3d-krzyzanowski-26wi', 'movement', 'At about 4 o\'clock the regiment rallied on Cemetery Hill and was ordered behind the stone fence', 'R263', q='At about 4 o\'clock the regiment rallied on Cemetery Hill', w='At about 4 o\'clock', t='1863-07-01T16:00', ap=True, pp='Cemetery Hill, behind the stone fence', gz='GZ-003', cf=['HW4', 'SC3'], note='Earlier than Howard (columns reached Cemetery Hill 4.30) and Schurz (after 5); also 3 p. m. arrival in the same report.'),
